  "slug": "scalable-commodity-1353",
  "summary": "Organ-resolved measurements now separate aging, cellular composition, and heritable adiposity within individual tissues.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread across these items is resolution of biological variation at the level of individual organs and anatomical compartments. Organ-specific proteomic aging clocks for eight mouse organs are applied to RNA and spatial transcriptomes, with age signals that depend on organ. ATLAS uses scRNA-seq-derived probe signatures to profile 40M cells across mouse brains and compare cell-type distributions across genetic backgrounds. A neural network localizes calvarial bone marrow in head MRI to estimate adiposity, with heritability, 41 genetic loci, and genetic correlations reported. These studies differ in modality and scope, so the shared element is spatial or organ-level stratification rather than a single method. What is new is the pairing of organ- or region-resolved readouts with genetic background or heritability analysis, as in the ATLAS and MRI items.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-04"
}
